{"name":"Inheritance","hex":"#d7ae77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"inheritance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The passing of title to an estate upon death.","That which a person is entitled to inherit, by law or testament, such as the part of an estate (i.e., a portion)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inheritance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Inheritance","blocks":[{"text":"Inheritance is the practice of receiving private property, titles, debts, entitlements, privileges, rights, and obligations upon the death of an individual. The rules of inheritance differ among societies and have changed over time. In legal terms, succession is the process by which a deceased person's rights and property are transferred to their heirs, while inheritance is the property or assets those heirs receive."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Shakespeare-Testament.jpg/330px-Shakespeare-Testament.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inheritance","wikidata":"Q200303"},{"title":"Inheritance (object-oriented programming)","blocks":[{"text":"In object-oriented programming, inheritance is the mechanism of basing an object or class upon another object or class, retaining similar implementation. It is also defined as deriving new classes from existing ones such as super class or base class and then forming them into a hierarchy of classes. In most class-based object-oriented languages like C++, an object created through inheritance, a \"child object\", acquires all the properties and behaviors of the \"parent object\", with the exception of: constructors, destructors, overloaded operators and friend functions of the base class. Inheritance allows programmers to create classes that are built upon existing classes, to specify a new implementation while maintaining the same behaviors, to reuse code and to independently extend original software via public classes and interfaces. The relationships of objects or classes through inheritance give rise to a directed acyclic graph."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inheritance_(object-oriented_programming)","wikidata":"Q212542"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/William_Hogarth_-_A_Rake%27s_Progress_-_Plate_1_-_The_Young_Heir_Takes_Possession_Of_The_Miser%27s_Effects.jpg/500px-William_Hogarth_-_A_Rake%27s_Progress_-_Plate_1_-_The_Young_Heir_Takes_Possession_Of_The_Miser%27s_Effects.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/William_Hogarth_-_A_Rake%27s_Progress_-_Plate_1_-_The_Young_Heir_Takes_Possession_Of_The_Miser%27s_Effects.jpg/500px-William_Hogarth_-_A_Rake%27s_Progress_-_Plate_1_-_The_Young_Heir_Takes_Possession_Of_The_Miser%27s_Effects.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"From William Hogarth's A Rake's Progress. \"The Young Heir Takes Possession Of The Miser's Effects\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWilliam_Hogarth_-_A_Rake's_Progress_-_Plate_1_-_The_Young_Heir_Takes_Possession_Of_The_Miser's_Effects.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Inheritance_by_amount_and_distribution_received_and_action_taken_with_inheritances_in_Great_Britain_between_2008_and_2010.png/500px-Inheritance_by_amount_and_distribution_received_and_action_taken_with_inheritances_in_Great_Britain_between_2008_and_2010.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Inheritance_by_amount_and_distribution_received_and_action_taken_with_inheritances_in_Great_Britain_between_2008_and_2010.png/500px-Inheritance_by_amount_and_distribution_received_and_action_taken_with_inheritances_in_Great_Britain_between_2008_and_2010.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inheritance by amount and distribution received and action taken with inheritances in Great Britain between 2008 and 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInheritance_by_amount_and_distribution_received_and_action_taken_with_inheritances_in_Great_Britain_between_2008_and_2010.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Single_Inheritance.jpg/250px-Single_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Single_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Single_Inheritance.jpg/250px-Single_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Single inheritance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASingle_Inheritance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Multiple_Inheritance.jpg/250px-Multiple_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/Multiple_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Multiple_Inheritance.jpg/250px-Multiple_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Multiple inheritance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMultiple_Inheritance.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Multilevel_Inheritance.jpg/250px-Multilevel_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/Multilevel_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Multilevel_Inheritance.jpg/250px-Multilevel_Inheritance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Multilevel inheritance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMultilevel_Inheritance.jpg"}],"sounds":{"inheritance":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/95/En-us-inheritance.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/95/En-us-inheritance.ogg/En-us-inheritance.ogg.mp3"}]}}}